sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: fleet maintenance redesign 2026-11-04, topology templates plan points 1 and 2. Replaces the task VM image build.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · after a release that changes Node state
  %% kind: template.refresh
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane I icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane T icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant I as Incus host<br/>holds templates
  participant T as Templates<br/>Gateway, dev, prod
  Note over GW: Release changed Node state<br/>task #5210
  %%> When:
  %%> - the release run ended verified, and its commit changed workflows, playbooks, role definitions, `recipe.json` or the release itself
  %%> - off the merge path: one refresh at a time; a newer release replaces a waiting one, so skipped commits never run
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-template-refresh
  SW->>T: Release onto the templates<br/>gateway:release:deploy · load
  SW->>T: Converge each Node<br/>node:converge · dev · prod
  %%> Why the normal commands:
  %%> - the templates get the release the same way the fleet does, so a refresh also tests the rollout path
  SW->>T: Check with Doctor<br/>doctor · zero drift
  SW->>I: Snapshot the templates<br/>incus snapshot · keep previous
  %%> Why only now:
  %%> - a failed refresh leaves the last good snapshots in place; clones and task VMs keep using them
  SW->>I: Publish the task VM image<br/>app-dev → Incus hosts
  %%> Why:
  %%> - task VMs boot from the app-dev template; there is no separate image build
  %%> - one template set lives on one Incus host; the other hosts get a copy of the image, a few minutes later
  alt refresh succeeds
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded
    Note over GW: Record template release
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code
    Note over GW: Keep the last snapshots<br/>alert template_refresh_failed
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - the next release refreshes again; the nightly build reports the cause
  end
